[19.401072, "o", "finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1190\r\nExploit Public-Facing Application\r\n[initial-access] step 1: Jenkins RCE\r\n(CVE-2024-23897)\r\nT1059.004 Unix Shell\r\n[execution] step 2: Groovy/shell\r\nexecution\r\nT1496\r\nResource Hijacking\r\n[impact] step 3: cryptomining\r\nT1037.004 RC Scripts\r\n[persistence] step 4: Groovy init\r\nhook\r\nT1098.004 SSH Authorized Keys\r\n[persistence] step 5:\r\nauthorized_keys backdoor\r\nT1053.003 Cron\r\n[execution] step 6: cron persistence\r\nT1070.002 Clear Linux or Mac System Logs\r\n[defense-evasion] step 7: Jenkins\r\nlog truncation\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\nCVE-2024-23897 CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1 CWE=CWE-22,CWE-27\r\nJenkins 2.441 and earlier, LTS 2.426.2 and earlier does not disable a feature of its CLI\r\ncommand parser that replaces an ’@’ character followed by a file path in an argument with the\r\nfile’s contents, allowing unauthenticated attackers to re\r\nref: http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/176839/Jenkins-2.441-LTS-2.426.3-CVE-2024-23897\r\n-Scanner.html\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.98\r\nc2 update-jenkins[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]jenkins[.]evil[:]3333\r\nwallet 4A0000000000000000003d98ef6bc04b\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S.\r\nNational Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\r\n"]
